// Package apiclient is the Go client of the Clarae notanda Cloud REST API,
// generated from api/openapi.yaml (ADR-0037 §3): one Go type per schema,
// parameter structs, request builders (NewXxxRequest), a Client with one method
// per operation and a ClientWithResponses whose XxxWithResponse methods return
// the parsed XxxReply (the suffix avoids clashes with schemas such as
// CommitResponse).
//
// apiclient.gen.go is generated by `task gen-openapi` with
// api/oapi-codegen-client.yaml and must not be edited by hand; `task check-gen`
// fails when it is out of date. The admin operations are left out (only the
// Web UI uses them, through @clarae/api-client), and so are the routes
// outside the contract: tus uploads and the SSE stream (/events).
//
// The package is deliberately thin: it builds requests and decodes payloads but
// knows nothing about authentication, retries, idempotency keys or problem
// documents. Those belong to the caller's HttpRequestDoer and wrapper; the
// desktop and WebAssembly core use apps/desktop/internal/sync/transport, which
// plugs its retrying, authenticating pipeline in with WithHTTPClient and turns
// application/problem+json bodies into typed errors. Keep the package free of
// platform-specific dependencies: it is compiled to js/wasm as well.
package apiclient
